#### 3. Sleepy Test
**Academic name:** Sleepy Test (Peruma et al., ESEC/FSE 2020)
**Affected test:** `ProcessOrder_AsyncNotification_IsSent` (line 98)

```csharp
processor.ProcessOrderAsync(order);
Thread.Sleep(2000);
Assert.IsTrue(_email.WasNotificationSent(order.Id));
```

**Risk:** Adds 2 seconds of wall-clock time per run. The delay may be too short on slow CI agents (flaky failure) or wastefully long on fast machines. Correlated with flaky tests (Camara et al., SAST 2021).

**Fix — await the async operation or use a deterministic signal:**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public async Task ProcessOrder_AsyncNotification_IsSent()
{
    var processor = new OrderProcessor(_db, _email, _inventory);
    var order = new Order { Items = { new OrderItem("SKU-1", 1) } };

    await processor.ProcessOrderAsync(order);

    Assert.IsTrue(_email.WasNotificationSent(order.Id));
}
```

