#### 7. Sensitive Equality
**Academic name:** Sensitive Equality (Peruma et al., ESEC/FSE 2020)
**Affected test:** `GetOrderSummary_ReturnsFormattedString` (line 135)

```csharp
Assert.AreEqual("Order ORD-001: 1 item(s), Total: $99.99", summary.ToString());
```

**Risk:** If the `ToString()` format changes (e.g., currency symbol, spacing, pluralization), the test breaks even though the underlying summary is correct. Couples the test to a display representation.

**Fix — assert on structured properties instead:**
```csharp
var summary = processor.GetOrderSummary(order);

Assert.AreEqual("ORD-001", summary.OrderId);
Assert.AreEqual(1, summary.ItemCount);
Assert.AreEqual(99.99m, summary.Total);
```

