#### 10. Assertion Roulette
**Academic name:** Assertion Roulette (van Deursen et al., 2001; Peruma et al., ESEC/FSE 2020)
**Affected test:** `CalculateTotal_ReturnsCorrectAmount` (lines 84–86)

```csharp
Assert.AreEqual(247.50m, order.TotalAmount);   // which one failed?
Assert.AreEqual(22.28m, order.TaxAmount);
Assert.AreEqual(269.78m, order.GrandTotal);
```

**Risk:** 3 assertions with no message parameters. If any fails, the test runner reports `Assert.AreEqual failed. Expected:<X>. Actual:<Y>.` with no indication of *which* value (subtotal? tax? total?) was wrong.

**Fix — add message parameters:**
```csharp
Assert.AreEqual(247.50m, order.TotalAmount, "Subtotal mismatch");
Assert.AreEqual(22.28m, order.TaxAmount, "Tax mismatch");
Assert.AreEqual(269.78m, order.GrandTotal, "Grand total mismatch");
```

